; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR BREAKOUT  -  knock out the wall, keep the ball in play   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot, press SPACE. Arrow keys (or a / d) move the paddle along the
; bottom; the ball knocks out a brick each time it reaches one. Reverse-video
; bricks score 5, '######' 3, '======' 1. Where the ball strikes the paddle
; sets its angle: the ends send it out wide, the middle steep. Three balls;
; clear the wall and a new one comes, faster. Each serve's first drop to
; the paddle is 25% slower, to give you time to get there. P pauses, ESC
; quits, SPACE plays again. BEST is kept while it runs.
;
; Which brick a cell belongs to is three table reads - no divide; each ball
; step is one PRINTSTR (blank the old cell, draw the new), each paddle move
; another.
;
; VT100: cursor addressing, erase to end of line, reverse video, hide/show
; cursor. No scrolling.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/breakout_verify.py, V0061.34): PASS 2026-10-01 - 3 autopilot games (ball, bricks, score checked against a model every step), a wall cleared, ball L1 5.0 .. L9 9.6 lines/s with each serve's first drop 23-25% slower, hands-off game over, paddle limits + 60/60 random-moment arrows, pause, restart, quit, rerun from dirty RAM.
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-10-01 - Craig: "Breakout works well now."
;
; 423 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 4005 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: the index for patching strings
; D 4009 11 0C 0E 64    LOADXI R12 0E64
; D 400D 11 0A 00 00    LOADXI R10 0000
; D 4011 3A 02 AC       COPYXMY R10 -> M(R12)              BEST = 0 (each time the program starts)
